{# Pirate-radio tuner widget. Pinned bottom-right of the viewport on every page
   (mirroring graph-widget.njk, which sits top-right). Behavior:
     - Four "bands" (ALPHA / BETA / GAMMA / DELTA), each with 256 hex frequencies
       displayed as 0xXX.XX.
     - Most frequencies are dead_air (static); a minority carry carrier_wave,
       transmission, or lock signals. Signal type per frequency is deterministic
       (hash of band+index) so the same dial position always sounds the same.
     - Audio is gated behind the power toggle to satisfy browser autoplay policy:
       the first user gesture (clicking power) unlocks AudioContext / speechSynthesis.
   JS lives at /assets/js/radio-widget.js. CSS in /assets/css/radio.css. #}


<aside
  class="radio-widget"
  id="radio-widget"
  aria-label="Pirate radio tuner"
  data-band="ALPHA"
  data-frequency="0"
>
  <div class="radio-widget-header">
    {# Fold button is the leftmost header element so it stays visible
       when the widget translates right and only a thin strip remains
       at the window edge. Clicking toggles the .is-folded class. #}
    <button
      type="button"
      class="radio-widget-fold"
      id="radio-widget-fold"
      aria-pressed="false"
      title="Fold scanner to right margin"
      aria-label="Fold scanner"
    >»</button>
    <span class="radio-widget-band" id="radio-widget-band">ALPHA</span>
    <span class="radio-widget-freq" id="radio-widget-freq">0x00</span>
    <button
      type="button"
      class="radio-widget-trawl"
      id="radio-widget-trawl"
      aria-pressed="false"
      title="Trawl — auto-scan the band, lingering on any non-static channel"
      aria-label="Trawl"
    >trawl</button>
    <button
      type="button"
      class="radio-widget-power"
      id="radio-widget-power"
      aria-pressed="false"
      title="Power"
      aria-label="Power"
    >◯</button>
  </div>

  <div class="radio-widget-bands" role="group" aria-label="Band selector">
    <button type="button" data-band="ALPHA" aria-pressed="true">α</button>
    <button type="button" data-band="BETA" aria-pressed="false">β</button>
    <button type="button" data-band="GAMMA" aria-pressed="false">γ</button>
    <button type="button" data-band="DELTA" aria-pressed="false">δ</button>
  </div>

  {# Dial + resume-prompt overlay share a relative wrapper so the overlay
     can sit exactly on top of the canvas. The overlay is shown only when
     the page reloads with powered=true but the AudioContext is still
     suspended (browser autoplay policy). Clicking it — or anywhere else —
     dismisses it and rebuilds the audio engine in the gesture-blessed
     context. See attemptAudioResumeOnGesture() in radio-widget.js. #}
  <div class="radio-widget-dial-wrap">
    <canvas
      id="radio-widget-dial"
      class="radio-widget-dial"
      tabindex="0"
      aria-label="Tuning dial. Click to coarse-tune, scroll or arrow keys to fine-tune."
    ></canvas>
    <button
      type="button"
      class="radio-widget-resume"
      id="radio-widget-resume"
      aria-label="Signal interrupted. Tap to resume."
      hidden
    >
      <span class="radio-widget-resume-line">signal interrupted</span>
      <span class="radio-widget-resume-cta">▸ tap to resume</span>
    </button>
  </div>

  <div class="radio-widget-status">
    <span id="radio-widget-status">offline</span>
  </div>
</aside>
